{{-- Marketing chrome. Layout group 'marketing'.

     This file is a FRAGMENT, not a document. stx synthesises <!DOCTYPE>, <html lang>,
     <head> and <body> from config/ui.ts app.head merged with each page's head — see
     generateDocumentShell. Writing a DOCTYPE or an html tag here (even inside a
     comment, because the test is an unanchored regex over the rendered string) makes
     hasDocumentShell() true, turns ensureDocumentShell into a no-op, and every page's
     title/description is dropped on the floor. Never add one.

     Comments here are {{-- --}}, which are removed before any gate runs. An HTML
     comment would survive into the response and be re-parsed by four separate
     consumers downstream.

     The name of this file IS the router's layout group: crossing between 'marketing'
     and the app shell makes the router do a full-document swap, which is the only
     path that carries stylesheet links across a navigation. --}}

@head
{{-- Marketing-only. Deliberately NOT in config/ui.ts app.head, which is global and
     would push these onto the 5 app/auth pages that intentionally do without them. --}}
<meta name="theme-color" content="#0a0c0e">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/marketing.css">
@stack('styles')
@endhead

@include('site-nav')

{{-- The single router container. Pages must NOT declare their own <main>: fragment
     extraction slices from the first <main> to the LAST </main>, so a second one
     makes the router swap the wrong span and duplicate the chrome. --}}
<main>
@yield('content')
</main>

@include('site-footer')

@stack('scripts')
